WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.521 --> 00:00:15.522
Smoke filled the stable.

2
00:00:16.142 --> 00:00:18.144
The other horses were restless and coughing.

3
00:00:20.366 --> 00:00:24.169
It was dark, and all the smoke made it impossible to see what was happening.

4
00:00:24.709 --> 00:00:25.490
I coughed again.

5
00:00:27.591 --> 00:00:28.532
It was hard to breathe.

6
00:00:30.054 --> 00:00:32.836
The crackling and snapping sound overhead was getting louder.

7
00:00:34.836 --> 00:00:37.337
I didn't know what it was, but it terrified me.

8
00:00:39.178 --> 00:00:40.959
I think it scared the other horses too.

9
00:00:42.319 --> 00:00:45.901
They all started stamping, whinnying, or kicking at their stalls.

10
00:00:48.202 --> 00:00:49.882
I heard rushing footsteps outside.

11
00:00:51.183 --> 00:00:53.564
A moment later the younger stable worker burst in.

12
00:00:54.624 --> 00:00:57.085
The fresh air he brought with him made it easier to breathe.

13
00:00:57.926 --> 00:00:59.226
But I was still very frightened.

14
00:01:00.747 --> 00:01:03.608
The worker grabbed the first horse in the row and tried to lead her out.

15
00:01:04.588 --> 00:01:07.329
But that horse was as scared as I was and refused to go.

16
00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:12.031
After a moment the man gave up and went to the next stall.

17
00:01:13.412 --> 00:01:16.313
But that horse pulled back as well, and so did the next.

18
00:01:18.514 --> 00:01:20.314
Finally the man came to my stall.

19
00:01:20.935 --> 00:01:23.856
He darted in and reached for my halter, but I whirled away.

20
00:01:25.937 --> 00:01:28.178
When he tried again, he managed to grab it.

21
00:01:29.018 --> 00:01:30.619
He gave a tug for me to follow.

22
00:01:31.479 --> 00:01:33.740
I refused, planting my feet where they were.

23
00:01:34.876 --> 00:01:37.859
I didn't know him, and I was too frightened to trust a stranger.

24
00:01:38.319 --> 00:01:39.480
I wasn't going anywhere!

25
00:01:41.482 --> 00:01:43.163
Now I realize how foolish that was.

26
00:01:44.084 --> 00:01:46.646
The stable worker was only trying to rescue all the horses.

27
00:01:47.887 --> 00:01:50.309
But at the time we were out of our minds with fear.

28
00:01:52.911 --> 00:01:58.155
That terrible crackling sound was all around, and it seemed safer to stay in my stall than risk

29
00:01:58.215 --> 00:01:59.956
getting closer to whatever was causing it.

30
00:02:02.038 --> 00:02:06.141
My stall had always been a safe place, whether at home or on the road.

31
00:02:07.342 --> 00:02:09.363
How was I to know that it was different this time?

32
00:02:10.524 --> 00:02:11.784
Finally the worker gave up.

33
00:02:12.645 --> 00:02:14.846
He rushed out of the stable again, shouting for help.

34
00:02:16.027 --> 00:02:18.949
A moment later the old man with the crooked leg came in.

35
00:02:20.009 --> 00:02:21.970
He was much calmer than the other man had been.

36
00:02:23.491 --> 00:02:26.273
He walked up to the first horse and talked to her softly.

37
00:02:27.354 --> 00:02:30.676
A second later the mare went with him, though she still looked anxious.

38
00:02:33.728 --> 00:02:37.190
The old man led her outside, then returned and went to the second horse.

39
00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:41.432
At the same time, James hurried in and came to my stall.

40
00:02:41.452 --> 00:02:47.096
"Come, my beauties, it's time to get out of here," he said to Ginger and me in his

41
00:02:47.196 --> 00:02:48.777
usual calm, cheerful voice.

42
00:02:50.017 --> 00:02:53.239
I was glad to see him, but I was still feeling very nervous.

43
00:02:54.460 --> 00:02:58.442
James pulled the scarf from around his neck and slipped it over my eyes so I couldn't see

44
00:02:58.502 --> 00:03:04.998
anything. I still heard the fire crackling, but the sound of James talking softly to me was closer

45
00:03:05.158 --> 00:03:06.179
and much more familiar.

46
00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.782
I decided to trust James and let him tell me what to do.

47
00:03:11.183 --> 00:03:13.504
After all, he had never let me down before.

48
00:03:14.805 --> 00:03:18.948
So I allowed him to lead me out, and a moment later, there was fresh air all around

49
00:03:19.028 --> 00:03:23.191
me. "Somebody hold this horse while I go back in!"

50
00:03:23.572 --> 00:03:26.974
James called, pulling the scarf off my eyes so I could see again.

51
00:03:28.155 --> 00:03:32.038
A man stepped up to take me, and James ran back into the burning stable.

52
00:03:33.739 --> 00:03:38.702
I was still feeling scared and uncertain, and I didn't want him to go, so I whinnied after

53
00:03:38.742 --> 00:03:43.145
him. Later Ginger told me that my whinny was what had saved her.

54
00:03:44.646 --> 00:03:49.049
Knowing that I was outside, she found the courage to follow James out of her stall.

55
00:03:50.030 --> 00:03:51.751
Through the smoke I watched the doorway.

56
00:03:52.872 --> 00:03:55.373
A moment later James and Ginger appeared in the doorway.

57
00:03:56.714 --> 00:03:58.836
By now the entire roof was blazing.

58
00:04:00.308 --> 00:04:02.210
We could hear things collapsing inside.

59
00:04:04.131 --> 00:04:06.633
Someone called out that the fire engine was on its way.

60
00:04:07.714 --> 00:04:09.916
The little old man was bringing other horses out.

61
00:04:10.777 --> 00:04:12.458
But we didn't stay to watch any longer.

62
00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:19.203
The squire had appeared, and he and James led Ginger and me to a different hotel.

63
00:04:21.005 --> 00:04:23.867
In the morning all the humans were talking about what had happened.

64
00:04:24.868 --> 00:04:29.151
The stable workers had gotten most of the other horses out, but two had been lost in the

65
00:04:29.212 --> 00:04:34.902
fire. I was glad that Ginger and I were safe in a different hotel stable, but I felt

66
00:04:34.982 --> 00:04:36.302
sad about those two horses.

67
00:04:37.503 --> 00:04:40.584
Everyone was sure that the young man's pipe had started the blaze.

68
00:04:41.685 --> 00:04:45.826
He said he'd put the pipe down before going up into the loft, just as the stable worker

69
00:04:45.866 --> 00:04:46.407
had asked.

70
00:04:47.647 --> 00:04:48.628
But nobody believed him.

71
00:04:50.708 --> 00:04:53.970
I was very glad that John had a strict rule at home about such things.

72
00:04:55.150 --> 00:04:58.792
Nobody was allowed to have a pipe or any other fire anywhere near the stable.

73
00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:02.766
I couldn't understand why that wasn't a rule at every stable.

74
00:05:05.591 --> 00:05:07.775
It certainly would have saved those two poor horses.
